<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>My Practice Page</title>
    <!-- FONTS -->
    <!-- Headers, Paragraphs and Figcaptions -->
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Edu+NSW+ACT+Cursive:wght@400..700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <!-- Titles -->
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Edu+NSW+ACT+Cursive:wght@400..700&family=Merriweather:ital,opsz,wght@0,18..144,300..900;1,18..144,300..900&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    
    <!-- CSS Style Rules to apply the font and responsive scaling -->
    <style>
      /* Centering layout on the page background */
      body {
          margin: 0;
          padding: 20px;
          min-height: 100vh;
          display: flex;
          justify-content: center;
          align-items: center;
          box-sizing: border-box;
          background-color: #f5f5f5;
      }

      /* Font Families */
      h2, h3, h4, p, figcaption {
          font-family: "Edu NSW ACT Cursive", cursive;
      }
     /* STICKY HEADER RULES */
      h1 {
          font-family: "Merriweather", serif;
          position: sticky;       /* Locks the element in place when scrolling */
          top: 0;                 /* Sticks it to the very top edge of the window */
          z-index: 100;           /* Forces it to stay floating on top of images */
          background-color: #CC0000; /* Matches background color so text underneath doesn't bleed through */
          width: 100%;
          max-width: 600px;       /* Matches your card width */
          margin: 0;
          padding: 20px 0;        /* Adds clean spacing around the text */
          text-align: center;
      }
      h4 {
          font-weight: normal; /* Makes h4 regular weight instead of bold */
      }

      /* Responsive container that keeps text locked to image width */
      .card {
          width: 100%;
          max-width: 600px; /* Limits size on desktop, scales fluidly on mobile */
          display: block;
      }

      /* Forces all images inside the card to scale responsively */
      .card img, .responsive-img {
          width: 100%;
          height: auto;
          display: block;
          margin-top: 15px;
      }

      /* Clean spacing between the two figure sections */
      figure {
          margin: 0 0 40px 0;
          padding: 0;
      }
      figure:last-child {
          margin-bottom: 0;
      }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
  <section style="text-align: center;" class="card">
    <figure>  
    <h1>The Atlan Expedition</h1>
    <h2>My Adventures On The CB500X</h2>
    <h3>My first ride on dirt and with street tyres no less.</h3>
    <h4 style="text-align: left;">Blackdown Tablelands,</h4>
    <p style="text-align: left;">It was intimidating to start with but I'd already gotten some good advice online about standing, essentailly "stand when you don't want to and sit when it's easy".</p>
    <p style="text-align: left;">The corrogation didn't help with the street tyres and pressures, I was slowing to a crawl around corners to avoid slipping on the gravel, keep in mind this was before I'd gotten any protection for me or the bike.</p>
    <img src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TheAtlanExpedition/CB500X-Adventures/refs/heads/main/Images/20260704_122043.jpg" alt="CB500X on the way up blackdown tablelands." class="responsive-img">
    <p style="text-align: left;">There were some great views around Blackdown Tablelands, this was on the way up the mountain on the side of the sealed road was a pitstop with some stones arranged for an unofficial camp fire.</p>
    <p style="text-align: left;">At the top of the mountain was an incredible view a short walk from the rest stop just before the road turned to dirt.</p>
    <img src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TheAtlanExpedition/CB500X-Adventures/refs/heads/main/Images/20260704_111719.jpg" alt="View from top of Blackdown Tablelands." class="responsive-img">
    </figure>      
  </section>  

</body>
</html>
